 # Replay spool format
 
-TBD.
+Run files start with `RUN_MAGIC`, then a stream of length-framed records —
+a u32 big-endian length prefix followed by the record bytes — and end with
+a record-count + SHA-256 footer computed over the framed stream.
+
+Record payloads use our compact custom binary codec; there is no JSON
+anywhere on the write path. Protobuf bar bytes are stored raw inside the
+record, so even a full-population spool (tens of millions of bars) stays
+comfortably within one scratch volume at roughly the size of the raw
+protobuf data plus framing overhead.
